  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000119773,
      "SummaryText": "The Calistoga Resiliency Center is a hybrid power generation facility that is being commissioned to provide backup power to the nearby town of Calistoga, CA.  Under normal conditions the site will remain off-line and idle until called upon by the local utility company to provide power to the town.  Given this scenario, the site, and in particular the hydrogen element, will only be fully operational for brief periods of a few days during a typical year.\n\nThe facility is a combination of a typical battery energy storage system (BESS) integrated with a newly developed hydrogen generation element.  The hydrogen element of the site utilizes several large stationary hydrogen fuel cell units, which were developed by an industry leading supplier of hydrogen products, paired with a large vacuum-insulated liquid hydrogen storage tank to provide continuous base load power to the system, and consequently, the local community.\n\nThe site, which sits on less than one acre of land, houses all the major equipment needed for the self-contained operation of the facility.  These major equipment items include the hydrogen fuel cell units, battery containers, power inverters, power transformers, central control house, air supply system, liquid hydrogen storage tank, vaporizers, and other balance of plant hardware.  The site property is enclosed in a security fence, with an 18 ft high rated CMU fire wall surrounding the hydrogen distribution area."
    }
  ]
